1
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:19,900
Cinderella's Sister

2
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:25,600
Episode 8

3
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:38,600
Joon Soo.

4
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:44,200
Was he moved to a larger hospital in Seoul? Is the surgery over?

5
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:47,800
Not yet?

6
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:53,900
Hyo Seon and I will get on the first flight tomorrow.

7
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,800
Everything we did here went well.

8
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:00,600
Are you listening?

9
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:05,600
Hyo Seon did it. If it wasn't for her, it wouldn't have worked.

10
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:09,400
Just focus and wait.

11
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:16,200
It's possible for things like that to happen at his age. Because we responded quickly, nothing bad will happen.

12
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,200
Hello? Hello?

13
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,900
Eun Jo? Eun Jo!

14
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:31,000
Eun Jo... Are you listening?

15
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:35,400
Is it because... of me?

16
00:01:46,400 --> 00:01:52,300
There's no chance. I didn't come all the way here to collapse now.

17
00:01:53,200 --> 00:02:00,300
Try it. Jesus, Buddha, the dieties.

18
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:03,800
If you're going to do something, try it.

19
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:09,800
If you've jam-packed my life on accident with all the misfortune

20
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:12,800
you should've spread out to others,

21
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:17,300
you should know what kind of wretch I am.

22
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:22,400
I can't stop here. I won't.

23
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:30,000
Hyo Seon, just like what they said

24
00:02:32,690 --> 00:02:35,430
because my mom and I

25
00:02:37,460 --> 00:02:40,990
only bring misfortune...

26
00:02:45,030 --> 00:02:47,850
are we eating up

27
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:53,300
ordinary people?

28
00:03:03,140 --> 00:03:07,810
There's no need to worry. The surgery went well, and the critical period has passed.

29
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,400
Of course.

30
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:13,900
Excuse me?

31
00:03:14,710 --> 00:03:17,970
Did you think something bad would happen?

32
00:03:28,400 --> 00:03:34,100
Dad collapsed with acute myocardial infarction caused by psychogenic shock,

33
00:03:34,100 --> 00:03:39,900
he almost died after getting emergency surgery.

34
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:46,000
I'm not there, but here.

35
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:51,000
Please think a bit about who should be the most consoled right now.

36
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:56,500
You should try to get some rest. Sleep here. I'll come wake you up.

37
00:04:49,750 --> 00:04:51,760
Dad?

38
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:56,600
Dad...

39
00:04:57,500 --> 00:05:02,100
Why did you do that? Why?

40
00:05:03,400 --> 00:05:05,700
Why did you do that?

41
00:05:15,700 --> 00:05:18,700
Don't cry. He's already having a difficult time.

42
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:41,600
Let's head in now.

43
00:05:41,600 --> 00:05:48,000
I'm okay. The weather is nice, and so is the breeze.

44
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:50,400
They said you shouldn't push yourself.

45
00:05:50,400 --> 00:05:52,900
I'm telling you I'm fine.

46
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:57,500
You can't. You should listen, Dear.

47
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:06,200
I'm really okay.

48
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:10,300
They said not to! Why won't you listen?

49
00:06:14,500 --> 00:06:16,600
You can't.

50
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:24,000
Okay. I'll listen then.

51
00:06:56,400 --> 00:07:00,600
How many times do I have to tell you? I said no salt.

52
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:05,300
The doctors said he can't have salty foods, why won't you listen?

53
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:07,600
It's not salty...

54
00:07:07,600 --> 00:07:11,400
What? Not salty? I'm telling you it's salty, but not salty?

55
00:07:11,400 --> 00:07:15,600
Are you saying that I'm calling something not salty, salty? Are you telling me I'm a crazy person?

56
00:07:15,600 --> 00:07:18,600
That's not what I meant ...

57
00:07:18,600 --> 00:07:22,000
We'll redo it. We were wrong, okay? We did wrong.

58
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:24,800
We'll completely remake it,

59
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:27,800
so please don't be angry, Joon Soo's mom.

60
00:07:28,800 --> 00:07:34,000
Joon Soo's Mom? Are you my senior?

61
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:39,400
I'm sorry, ma'am. I did wrong. We'll hurry up and remake it.

62
00:07:41,380 --> 00:07:43,980
Bring me the boiled seaweed. I'm going to remake it.

63
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:49,000
Um, excuse me... We're all out of the boiled seaweed...

64
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:09,600
Hyo Seon! What brings you here, without even calling?

65
00:08:09,600 --> 00:08:12,400
Can you give me one set of the best hiking clothes?

66
00:08:12,400 --> 00:08:15,600
Hey. It's been so long, but you won't even greet me?

67
00:08:15,600 --> 00:08:20,600
If you head right into the point like that, I'm grateful.

68
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:23,100
Who's going to wear it? Are you going to hike?

69
00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:26,000
No. It's for my dad.

70
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,000
Your dad?

71
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:32,000
When he gets better, he needs to exercise a bit.

72
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:34,700
I see... But...

73
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:39,500
Well, sure! Having two sets won't hurt. Follow me.

74
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:42,700
Two sets? What do you mean?

75
00:08:42,700 --> 00:08:45,800
A little while ago, your sister bought a set of clothes.

76
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:48,500
Eun Jo, your sister.

77
00:08:49,600 --> 00:08:54,400
While you were in the hospital, we signed contracts with 7 top luxury hotels in Tokyo.

78
00:08:54,400 --> 00:08:57,300
And we have completed the third delivery today.

79
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:02,520
It'll go well. It will become a sign of the future.

80
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:06,800
I'm happy that you're here.

81
00:09:06,800 --> 00:09:11,500
Does your father know that you're here?

82
00:09:13,600 --> 00:09:18,400
He doesn't, does he? Let me meet your father.

83
00:09:18,400 --> 00:09:19,400
What?

84
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:25,400
When you were young, taking you in was an adult taking care of a child.

85
00:09:25,400 --> 00:09:29,200
It was something that I could do and it was doable.

86
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:32,700
But right now, I seem like I have no conscience.

87
00:09:32,700 --> 00:09:34,400
Ahjussi.

88
00:09:34,400 --> 00:09:40,400
For sure, your father also has other plans for you.

89
00:09:40,400 --> 00:09:46,400
That's why I can't hold you back

90
00:09:46,400 --> 00:09:48,800
Ahjussi, it's not like that.

91
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:52,800
What do you know, punk? Have you given birth to a child?

92
00:09:54,400 --> 00:10:00,300
Your father had said that he would not utter it.

93
00:10:00,300 --> 00:10:03,400
You can't suspect your father's heart.

94
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:06,800
My father is different from you.

95
00:10:06,800 --> 00:10:08,600
Of course he is different.

96
00:10:08,600 --> 00:10:15,400
Because he is different, he can protect that big company along with his many employees and family.

97
00:10:15,400 --> 00:10:17,200
That's not it.

98
00:10:17,200 --> 00:10:20,400
I should meet him to see if he is or isn't.

99
00:10:20,400 --> 00:10:25,600
Don't meet him. I will go and meet him.

100
00:10:25,600 --> 00:10:31,300
It will soon happen someday. Please let me do it.

101
00:10:32,200 --> 00:10:37,400
Okay. Not someday, but make sure it will happen.

102
00:10:38,400 --> 00:10:40,300
Ahjussi.

103
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:43,600
Say it.

104
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:47,200
You have to trust me.

105
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:54,400
Whatever happens, even if something unexpected happens.

106
00:10:54,400 --> 00:10:57,200
Please trust me.

107
00:11:00,600 --> 00:11:06,200
"Trust me" is such a nice phrase to hear. Even that kid Hyo Seong asks me to trust her.

108
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:11,100
And next is you? It's so dependable so it's all good.

109
00:11:14,400 --> 00:11:16,500
Where are you going?

110
00:11:16,500 --> 00:11:20,400
Meet the Japanese buyer alone or take Hyo Seong with you. I can't go.

111
00:11:20,400 --> 00:11:25,400
What are you saying? I purposely brought Gi Hoon to go with you.

112
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:38,500
Please be careful.

113
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:41,200
Here.

114
00:11:43,800 --> 00:11:46,100
I will be getting some.

115
00:11:51,400 --> 00:11:54,600
You came to get this? What are you going to do with it?

116
00:11:54,600 --> 00:11:56,600
I wanted to do some heat treatments with it.

117
00:11:56,600 --> 00:11:58,400
- Heat treatments?
- Yes.

118
00:11:58,400 --> 00:12:02,800
If we use heat to kill the harmful strains, we should be able to make a consistent liquor.

119
00:12:02,800 --> 00:12:08,200
If we were to succeed even if we don't ferment it separately then we can get a better alcohol.

120
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:11,800
Then, we can reduce the processing time and it's possible we can reduce the cost of production.

121
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:15,600
Wait, wait. If you apply heat treatments,

122
00:12:15,600 --> 00:12:20,000
Will it only kill just the harmful ones? Wouldn't it also weaken the good yeast strains too?

123
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:24,000
We just have to adjust the fermentation environment. I need to go now.

124
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:25,900
Go on in.

125
00:12:26,600 --> 00:12:28,200
Eun Jo

126
00:12:30,960 --> 00:12:33,170
I'm wearing this.

127
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:36,400
Yes.

128
00:12:36,400 --> 00:12:38,300
Isn't it pretty?

129
00:12:40,100 --> 00:12:42,300
It is pretty, Dad!

130
00:12:44,600 --> 00:12:48,700
You are so cool. Unni bought you that?

131
00:12:49,900 --> 00:12:53,000
I also went to her store.

132
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:58,000
But Unni already bought it first.

133
00:12:58,800 --> 00:13:01,800
You picked a good color.

134
00:13:01,800 --> 00:13:04,200
She called multiple times.

135
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:08,000
She said to come since the store opened.

136
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:12,200
I couldn't dare not stop by since I went to Seoul on purpose.

137
00:13:12,800 --> 00:13:18,400
Unni, you bought the gift for Dad but why are you giving excuses to me?

138
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:23,000
As if you were afraid I would get mad if you said you did that because you were thinking of Dad?

139
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:27,600
Unni, I'm not 16 anymore.

140
00:13:27,600 --> 00:13:31,800
Dad. It's unfair because of Unni.

141
00:13:31,800 --> 00:13:36,600
That's right, it feels unfair to me too. So you just bought something from your friend's store

142
00:13:36,600 --> 00:13:41,000
and just tossed it to me?

143
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:43,100
I will be going now.

144
00:13:43,800 --> 00:13:46,200
Are you going to the lab?

145
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:49,700
Dad, let's take her there.

146
00:13:50,400 --> 00:13:54,800
He just came from there. He needs to rest now.

147
00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:59,500
Dad, it's okay, right? I will be the one driving.

148
00:14:00,350 --> 00:14:02,890
You need to go with Gi Hoon.

149
00:14:02,900 --> 00:14:09,780
Shall I go and see how good you are with dealing with the buyers?

150
00:14:18,200 --> 00:14:23,200
♫  Even if there are wounds left in my heart now ♫

151
00:14:25,600 --> 00:14:30,400
♫  I am told to forget about you ♫

152
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:39,400
♫  but even if I bite my lips and bear it ♫

153
00:14:39,400 --> 00:14:44,200
♫ My love, you are the only one.♫

154
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:48,000
The secret to the taste of the makgeoli ( rice wine)

155
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:51,500
is in a special yeast.

156
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:55,600
The yeast was created by my father.

157
00:14:55,600 --> 00:14:59,200
You're so cute. I would like to have a drink alone with you.

158
00:14:59,200 --> 00:15:02,600
Thank you for the compliment.

159
00:15:02,600 --> 00:15:08,800
♫ So I can't laugh ♫

160
00:15:08,800 --> 00:15:18,200
♫  I call out your name again ♫

161
00:15:40,400 --> 00:15:43,980
What? Say that again, Oppa.

162
00:15:43,980 --> 00:15:46,500
What did I do?

163
00:15:48,200 --> 00:15:50,200
Who taught you to act like that?

164
00:15:50,200 --> 00:15:52,800
That's why I'm asking what I did?

165
00:15:52,800 --> 00:15:57,000
Don't you know what it means "to have a drink separately?"

166
00:15:57,000 --> 00:16:01,900
For what reason did you agree for such a proposal? Are you that kind of girl?

167
00:16:02,800 --> 00:16:03,600
What?

168
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:08,000
I told you we are doing business and not selling alcohol.

169
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:12,400
Are you done talking?

170
00:16:12,400 --> 00:16:17,200
You didn't do business today. Know how to be ashamed.

171
00:16:25,500 --> 00:16:29,200
Then why did you accept the invitation then?

172
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:31,400
Why did you agree for us to go to her house, eat her food, drink with her,

173
00:16:31,400 --> 00:16:35,000
sign an autograph for that child and take a picture with him as well?!

174
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:38,400
I did that for a pitiful someone without a mother.

175
00:16:38,400 --> 00:16:41,000
I didn't sell my smile.

176
00:16:41,800 --> 00:16:43,700
What did you say?

177
00:16:46,200 --> 00:16:51,000
Then... are you saying I sold mine?

178
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:55,600
To those Japanese? Did I?

179
00:16:57,000 --> 00:17:00,800
Oppa! How could you...

180
00:17:00,800 --> 00:17:03,600
How could you say that to me?

181
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:06,000
Is that something you should be saying to me?

182
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:09,900
Is that something you really should be saying to me?

183
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:46,000
It's okay.

184
00:17:53,360 --> 00:17:55,460
Are you okay?

185
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:05,400
Are you okay?

186
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:21,300
- My heart...
- What?

187
00:18:22,200 --> 00:18:25,600
Your heart?

188
00:18:25,600 --> 00:18:27,400
Does it hurt?

189
00:18:28,500 --> 00:18:32,500
Are you having a hard time breathing?

190
00:18:36,700 --> 00:18:39,600
I'm asking if you are hurt?

191
00:18:40,800 --> 00:18:45,600
My heart is fluttering, Oppa.

192
00:18:45,600 --> 00:18:49,400
♫  Leaving behind the time ♫

193
00:18:49,400 --> 00:18:55,800
My heart is just... beating fast.

194
00:18:55,800 --> 00:19:00,800
♫  I said I longed for you ♫

195
00:19:00,800 --> 00:19:04,300
I'm shaking.

196
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:13,500
It's not cold but I'm shaking.

197
00:19:14,400 --> 00:19:18,000
♫  doesn't know that I longed for you ♫

198
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:27,400
♫  Looking only in this direction my two eyes ♫

199
00:19:28,800 --> 00:19:35,400
Move over to the driver's seat. I'm going to push from outside.

200
00:19:35,400 --> 00:19:41,000
♫  If I can always look at you ♫

201
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:49,600
♫  The day I return to your side again come again ♫

202
00:20:51,430 --> 00:20:55,350
I was wondering if you are eating since you haven't gone home in days.

203
00:20:57,470 --> 00:21:00,960
Ahjumma was curious if you were eating.

204
00:21:01,800 --> 00:21:03,700
Mom?

205
00:21:14,280 --> 00:21:16,090
Is it delicious?

206
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:18,800
Delicious, right?

207
00:21:18,800 --> 00:21:21,000
You can cook some.

208
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:25,000
It's not me. It's ahjumma.

209
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:29,200
My mom doesn't do these things. She hasn't done so for my whole life.

210
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:32,400
Why are you lying so uselessly?

211
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:37,600
My mom probably thinks I'm sleeping at home now.

212
00:21:37,600 --> 00:21:40,400
As if. Why would she?

213
00:21:41,200 --> 00:21:45,000
My mom, she doesn't know who you are, right?

214
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:50,100
That is... who would have imagined I grew up to be this handsome.

215
00:21:54,200 --> 00:21:59,830
You... how did you say you knew I was in this house?

216
00:22:03,800 --> 00:22:06,500
Dae Seong True Wine Makers Liquor, expanding quickly into the market.

217
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:20,400
- So?
- What?

218
00:22:20,400 --> 00:22:24,400
So? After you saw me in a magazine, what did you do?

219
00:22:24,400 --> 00:22:26,200
Ah, after that?

220
00:22:26,200 --> 00:22:31,400
I searched for the number and called asking to wait since I will seek employment after I get discharged.

221
00:22:31,400 --> 00:22:34,000
I kept calling twice a day.

222
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:37,500
Oh yeah, Hyungnim came home.

223
00:22:39,800 --> 00:22:45,200
Hyungnim, I just... committed a huge sin.

224
00:22:45,200 --> 00:22:49,600
I must have lost my mind for a while.

225
00:22:49,600 --> 00:22:54,000
I couldn't just be forever living in your shadows just leeching off of you...

226
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:57,800
and I just... wanted to use my strength to go on my own

227
00:22:57,800 --> 00:23:02,400
so I could stand shoulder-to-shoulder with you and compete fairly.

228
00:23:02,400 --> 00:23:06,200
You wanted to be independent from me.

229
00:23:06,200 --> 00:23:11,000
So you stole from me and made a fake?

230
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:16,400
That's why my head is not in the right place, Hyungnim.

231
00:23:16,400 --> 00:23:20,100
My brain wasn't good ever since birth.

232
00:23:20,100 --> 00:23:24,600
So that's why my father is to blame for all this. It's my father's fault.

233
00:23:24,600 --> 00:23:27,400
Because Father kept on being terrible to Mom.

234
00:23:27,400 --> 00:23:32,000
My mom wanted to get rid of me who is in her belly so she must have drank some soy sauce or vinegar.

235
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:33,000
Stand up.

236
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:37,200
It's not even just vinegar and soy cause but from what I've heard probably some pepper powder too...

237
00:23:37,200 --> 00:23:39,000
Stand up. Now!

238
00:23:41,600 --> 00:23:42,600
Yes, Hyungnim.

239
00:23:42,600 --> 00:23:46,400
Until when are you going to live like this? How old are you already?

240
00:23:46,400 --> 00:23:51,500
You are past the age of marriage and still living off your brother-in-law and causing trouble.

241
00:23:52,800 --> 00:23:55,200
I know, right.

242
00:23:55,200 --> 00:23:59,500
Do you think I wasn't thinking of you?

243
00:24:00,400 --> 00:24:03,800
You are Hyo Seong's only uncle.

244
00:24:03,800 --> 00:24:08,200
I was thinking of having you be independent and married off as part of my responsibility.

245
00:24:08,200 --> 00:24:12,900
You didn't know that and caused this trouble?

246
00:24:18,550 --> 00:24:22,990
- Hae Jin.
- Yes, Hyungnim.

247
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:27,800
Without me, what will you do?

248
00:24:29,000 --> 00:24:30,800
Pardon?

249
00:24:30,800 --> 00:24:33,800
No one knows what will happen.

250
00:24:33,800 --> 00:24:39,100
Without me, do you think it will be easy for you to stay in this house?

251
00:24:40,400 --> 00:24:43,500
Are you going somewhere, Hyungnim?

252
00:24:44,200 --> 00:24:46,700
Where are you going?

253
00:24:55,200 --> 00:24:59,400
Let go! Let go! Where are you taking me?

254
00:24:59,400 --> 00:25:03,300
Follow me! If you caused trouble then you should take responsibility.

255
00:25:03,300 --> 00:25:05,500
Let go!

256
00:25:06,200 --> 00:25:11,000
Jeong Woo! Tie him up. Tie him and bring him to the police station.

257
00:25:11,000 --> 00:25:12,400
What are you doing, Noona?

258
00:25:12,400 --> 00:25:14,540
No, Hyungnim isn't doing anything about it,

259
00:25:14,540 --> 00:25:17,400
so why are you making a fuss?

260
00:25:17,400 --> 00:25:18,830
Go and come with me to confess to the police.

261
00:25:18,830 --> 00:25:22,200
We've been branded completely as merchants who sell fake liquor right now.

262
00:25:22,200 --> 00:25:23,700
The factory has stopped!

263
00:25:23,700 --> 00:25:26,600
There are no orders coming in from anywhere in the country.

264
00:25:26,600 --> 00:25:27,600
Hurry and go!

265
00:25:27,600 --> 00:25:31,200
Let go! Won't you let this go! I said let go!

266
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:36,200
Take responsibility! Then we will be able to recover!

267
00:25:43,010 --> 00:25:44,860
Grab her.

268
00:25:57,000 --> 00:25:59,300
Hey! What are you doing?!

269
00:26:06,400 --> 00:26:09,000
Go with me! You should surrender.

270
00:26:09,000 --> 00:26:13,200
Go to the police station! If not I will report you!

271
00:26:13,200 --> 00:26:16,200
Who are you to tell my Uncle to turn himself in?

272
00:26:16,200 --> 00:26:19,600
My father has forgiven him!

273
00:26:22,800 --> 00:26:26,600
Turn yoursself in! Turn yourself in!

274
00:26:26,600 --> 00:26:30,400
Let's go to the police station. Turn yourself in!

275
00:26:30,400 --> 00:26:32,800
What is this girl?

276
00:26:32,800 --> 00:26:34,400
You'd better let go of her.

277
00:26:34,400 --> 00:26:36,500
What are you all doing?

278
00:27:40,600 --> 00:27:42,000
Let go! Let go!

279
00:27:42,000 --> 00:27:45,000
Okay. Okay. You need to breathe.

280
00:27:45,000 --> 00:27:48,800
Let me run for you. Where do you need to run to?

281
00:27:48,800 --> 00:27:51,000
Till there?

282
00:28:44,000 --> 00:28:47,000
You already forgot what upset you, right?

283
00:28:47,600 --> 00:28:50,800
Right. I did.

284
00:28:51,600 --> 00:28:52,400
Why?

285
00:28:52,400 --> 00:28:55,200
And your tears all went back, right?

286
00:28:57,000 --> 00:28:58,300
Yeah.

287
00:28:58,300 --> 00:29:02,500
Now, I can do a show, right?

288
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:16,300
One, two three...

289
00:29:17,200 --> 00:29:19,200
Watch.

290
00:29:59,600 --> 00:30:06,200
♫ Again today my memory led me astray♫

291
00:30:06,200 --> 00:30:11,900
♫ I who am strolling at the end of the street ♫

292
00:30:13,400 --> 00:30:20,600
♫  where you can't hold me again ♫

293
00:30:20,600 --> 00:30:26,400
♫  I ask again about the way. ♫

294
00:30:26,400 --> 00:30:35,000
♫ Saying I want to see you and hold you again ♫

295
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:41,200
♫ While looking at heaven I'm praying ♫

296
00:30:41,200 --> 00:30:48,600
♫ It must be you. I cannot be without you. ♫

297
00:30:48,600 --> 00:30:55,200
♫  Like this for another day, month or year ♫

298
00:30:55,200 --> 00:31:02,800
♫  I don't mind even if I am hurt. I don't mind even if my heart breaks ♫

299
00:31:02,800 --> 00:31:09,100
♫  Yes, if it's just you, it is enough ♫

300
00:31:11,000 --> 00:31:18,800
♫  because, yes, you are the only one I love. ♫

301
00:31:29,200 --> 00:31:33,000
Look carefully. This moment

302
00:31:33,000 --> 00:31:37,000
might be the moment that changes Daeseong's history.

303
00:31:39,030 --> 00:31:41,340
Isn't that right, Eun Jo?

304
00:32:03,400 --> 00:32:05,400
Makgeolli (Rice wine)
Test 1

305
00:34:24,200 --> 00:34:26,400
Let's proceed with Daeseong.

306
00:34:26,400 --> 00:34:28,600
Yes, I understand.

307
00:34:28,600 --> 00:34:33,600
But are you sure that it won't be risky? It could cause a problem...

308
00:34:55,000 --> 00:34:58,200
Are you crazy? Do you have a death wish?

309
00:34:58,200 --> 00:35:02,800
If the person who is calling me so late is not crazy, then what are you?

310
00:35:03,800 --> 00:35:08,000
You are the one who will wreck everything for me.

311
00:35:08,000 --> 00:35:10,600
Do you think I will be ruined alone?

312
00:35:10,600 --> 00:35:14,700
Even if I were to be ruined, I will kill you before I get ruined.

313
00:35:19,000 --> 00:35:21,300
What are you, brat!

314
00:35:32,100 --> 00:35:33,600
What's that?

315
00:35:33,600 --> 00:35:36,500
What do you mean? It's nothing.

316
00:35:37,600 --> 00:35:39,000
Give me your phone.

317
00:35:39,000 --> 00:35:41,600
What? Are you crazy?

318
00:35:41,600 --> 00:35:43,300
Who is that?

319
00:35:43,300 --> 00:35:45,400
You don't need to know.

320
00:35:50,400 --> 00:35:52,300
Is it Mr. Jang?

321
00:35:57,200 --> 00:36:00,600
Are you crazy? Why are you mentioning him all of a sudden?

322
00:36:00,600 --> 00:36:05,500
Then, is it a different man and not Mr. Jang?

323
00:36:06,200 --> 00:36:09,200
I'm hearing all sorts of things. You don't need to know.

324
00:36:09,200 --> 00:36:12,600
Mom. I could die.

325
00:36:14,200 --> 00:36:15,100
What!

326
00:36:15,100 --> 00:36:18,400
Let's say the containers that I have to be able to tolerate you

327
00:36:18,400 --> 00:36:22,200
are about a hundred small ones.

328
00:36:23,200 --> 00:36:27,000
And that one by one they are broken

329
00:36:28,400 --> 00:36:30,800
now there's only one left.

330
00:36:30,800 --> 00:36:33,000
What are you saying?

331
00:36:33,000 --> 00:36:36,500
And if that one breaks,

332
00:36:37,300 --> 00:36:42,100
I really... will not live.

333
00:36:42,800 --> 00:36:47,000
You btch! Btch! There really is nothing you can't say to your mother!

334
00:36:47,000 --> 00:36:49,800
What! You will not live? If you won't!

335
00:36:49,800 --> 00:36:52,600
No matter how towards Hyo Seon's dad

336
00:36:52,600 --> 00:36:55,800
you don't have any affection for him...

337
00:36:55,800 --> 00:36:58,300
You can't do that, Mom.

338
00:36:59,200 --> 00:37:02,300
That shouldn't be.

339
00:37:04,200 --> 00:37:07,000
To Hyo Seon's dad

340
00:37:07,000 --> 00:37:11,800
if you do something that shouldn't be done, I...

341
00:37:13,980 --> 00:37:17,530
I will go to hell instead of you.

342
00:37:20,000 --> 00:37:25,700
Hell... rather than what you are to me,

343
00:37:27,400 --> 00:37:30,000
would be easier to bear.

344
00:37:33,000 --> 00:37:35,200
I mean it.

345
00:38:11,400 --> 00:38:16,400
- Fine weather, isn't it?
- Fine weather, isn't it? (In Japanese)

346
00:38:16,400 --> 00:38:20,990
Isn't this type of weather pretty good?

347
00:38:20,990 --> 00:38:25,500
Isn't this type of weather pretty good?

348
00:38:30,400 --> 00:38:32,300
Aren't you going to look at the book?

349
00:38:34,000 --> 00:38:35,800
I am.

350
00:38:44,980 --> 00:38:48,580
If you are going to be like this then, I can't do anything with you.

351
00:38:51,800 --> 00:38:53,600
Oppa.

352
00:38:53,600 --> 00:38:56,200
I told you stop being immature.

353
00:38:59,200 --> 00:39:01,200
I am not.

354
00:39:01,200 --> 00:39:03,600
If not then what is it?

355
00:39:07,200 --> 00:39:11,000
I'm not a child.

356
00:39:11,000 --> 00:39:16,400
- What?
- Don't look at me like a child. It hurts my pride.

357
00:39:17,100 --> 00:39:20,400
Just because you saw me since I was a child, do you still see me as a child?

358
00:39:20,400 --> 00:39:25,200
Am I still a schoolgirl that loses stuff all over the place?

359
00:39:25,200 --> 00:39:28,000
I am speeding it up to be mature like an adult.

360
00:39:28,000 --> 00:39:31,200
I am trying hard to be like you!

361
00:39:31,200 --> 00:39:34,600
The one who is trying hard is not studying when she's supposed to be studying.

362
00:39:34,600 --> 00:39:37,000
I like you to death.

363
00:39:38,130 --> 00:39:39,960
What did you say?

364
00:39:40,600 --> 00:39:43,500
What can I do when I like you so much?

365
00:39:44,200 --> 00:39:48,200
Even if you get mad at me or scold me.

366
00:39:48,200 --> 00:39:52,800
Even if you dislike me, look down on me or laugh at me.

367
00:39:52,800 --> 00:39:57,500
Even though you insult me by saying that I am selling my smile.

368
00:39:57,500 --> 00:39:59,700
No matter what you do, I still like you.

369
00:40:00,400 --> 00:40:03,000
What should I do?

370
00:40:03,600 --> 00:40:08,400
If you're such an adult, tell me what to do at this time?

371
00:40:09,100 --> 00:40:11,600
Answer me now.

372
00:40:14,000 --> 00:40:19,300
You don't know, right? You probably don't.

373
00:40:20,800 --> 00:40:23,200
Because this isn't Japanese language,

374
00:40:23,200 --> 00:40:27,500
It's neither math nor management or something you can study.

375
00:40:29,500 --> 00:40:34,700
And also, because I am not Eun Jo.

376
00:40:36,190 --> 00:40:37,860
Right?

377
00:40:38,600 --> 00:40:42,400
Don't taint my name Goo Hyo Seon.

378
00:40:50,830 --> 00:40:55,340
I have nothing to do with you two.

379
00:40:56,600 --> 00:41:01,800
I am not like you who would have my heart hurt over a man.

380
00:41:01,800 --> 00:41:04,200
Do you know that?

381
00:41:04,200 --> 00:41:07,800
You know what kind of person I am.

382
00:41:08,600 --> 00:41:11,400
The moment I see what is in front of me

383
00:41:11,400 --> 00:41:15,100
that person has nothing to do with me.

384
00:41:16,200 --> 00:41:20,000
I... with people I have lived with before

385
00:41:20,000 --> 00:41:25,000
I am used to parting ways with them even with no warning.

386
00:41:25,000 --> 00:41:30,500
Those people whom I have lived with before become people whom I have nothing to do with in an instant.

387
00:41:31,540 --> 00:41:37,010
That... is the easiest thing in the world.

388
00:41:38,720 --> 00:41:44,220
Whether I eat with those people or be rained on.

389
00:41:45,600 --> 00:41:49,500
No matter how well they treat me, for me...

390
00:41:50,600 --> 00:41:55,600
throwing those people out is not hard at all.

391
00:41:58,800 --> 00:42:01,800
It's the same if someone throws me away.

392
00:42:03,000 --> 00:42:06,100
Even if they leave without a word.

393
00:42:06,100 --> 00:42:09,200
It's something that I am good at.

394
00:42:09,200 --> 00:42:13,700
I live while thinking, "they must be good at it too."

395
00:42:16,580 --> 00:42:19,290
Liking to death, that thing...

396
00:42:20,000 --> 00:42:23,000
I don't know about that as much as a cat or a dog would.

397
00:42:24,200 --> 00:42:26,900
So Goo Hyo Seon,

398
00:42:27,800 --> 00:42:33,000
don't drag me in. Just like to death on your own.

399
00:42:38,600 --> 00:42:40,600
Stop right there.

400
00:42:40,600 --> 00:42:42,600
Stop right there!

401
00:42:44,700 --> 00:42:46,200
Let go.

402
00:42:46,200 --> 00:42:48,000
Do you want to get scolded?

403
00:42:49,300 --> 00:42:52,000
If you want to get scolded then follow her.

404
00:43:14,930 --> 00:43:17,630
Eun Jo Test 1#

405
00:43:36,600 --> 00:43:38,900
Please ferment well.

406
00:43:40,800 --> 00:43:42,900
I beg you.

407
00:44:05,000 --> 00:44:07,000
Me too.

408
00:44:09,400 --> 00:44:15,600
I also, even for a second, parting ways with what stole my heart

409
00:44:15,600 --> 00:44:18,000
is nothing to me.

410
00:44:19,400 --> 00:44:24,000
So bad, being emotional for a moment.

411
00:44:24,000 --> 00:44:28,600
When I think of events of the past or the feelings I have in the past

412
00:44:28,600 --> 00:44:33,200
I do bring it up once in a while but that's it.

413
00:44:35,600 --> 00:44:37,900
For me also, just like you ...

414
00:44:40,200 --> 00:44:42,100
it's simple.

415
00:44:58,400 --> 00:45:02,400
I am like that, but you are not.

416
00:45:09,580 --> 00:45:13,940
You... lied.

417
00:45:16,200 --> 00:45:18,100
Don't.

418
00:45:19,470 --> 00:45:21,830
Don't hate me.

419
00:45:22,800 --> 00:45:25,990
You hating me to death,

420
00:45:27,000 --> 00:45:31,900
forcing to forget or to hate me, don't do that. Just don't do anything.

421
00:45:34,800 --> 00:45:36,900
Just...

422
00:45:39,300 --> 00:45:41,700
think I'm not here.

423
00:45:48,350 --> 00:45:50,170
I...

424
00:45:55,320 --> 00:45:59,820
owe so much to this family.

425
00:46:01,820 --> 00:46:05,400
If there is someone who would wreck this family,

426
00:46:06,810 --> 00:46:09,170
I will kill them all.

427
00:46:15,300 --> 00:46:18,000
If you do something bad to Hyo Seon

428
00:46:19,700 --> 00:46:22,400
know that you will die in my hands.

429
00:47:12,000 --> 00:47:14,000
Open it.

430
00:47:22,800 --> 00:47:23,800
Should I open it?

431
00:47:23,800 --> 00:47:27,400
No. I will.

432
00:48:05,400 --> 00:48:09,000
Scum has formed.

433
00:48:17,200 --> 00:48:21,600
The yeast is still alive. It's not completely ruined yet.

434
00:48:21,600 --> 00:48:26,800
- You should spread some flour...
- No. I will throw it away.

435
00:48:28,400 --> 00:48:33,000
Go and tell them to spread flour and set it aside. It will be fine to drink with the family.

436
00:48:33,000 --> 00:48:35,700
I said I will throw it away!

437
00:49:05,400 --> 00:49:08,800
It's something that Dad was not able to do.

438
00:49:08,800 --> 00:49:11,800
Did you think you would be able to do it?

439
00:49:20,400 --> 00:49:26,000
Dad... because he let you be

440
00:49:26,000 --> 00:49:30,700
did you think he believed that you would succeed?

441
00:49:32,110 --> 00:49:36,290
Can you be quiet? It's noisy.

442
00:49:37,380 --> 00:49:42,800
You... want to be a heroine, right?

443
00:49:44,800 --> 00:49:50,600
If you go ta-da and discover a yeast strain that's publishable

444
00:49:50,600 --> 00:49:53,800
then the factory that my uncle ruined

445
00:49:53,800 --> 00:49:56,400
you'd be able to say that you'd saved it.

446
00:49:57,100 --> 00:49:59,800
You wanted to boast, right?

447
00:50:03,400 --> 00:50:05,100
What to do?

448
00:50:07,800 --> 00:50:10,000
The heroine is not you.

449
00:50:11,500 --> 00:50:16,000
The buyer that I met has placed an order today.

450
00:50:16,000 --> 00:50:21,100
Big enough to the extent that we're not able to fill that order because we don't have enough equipment, and

451
00:50:21,100 --> 00:50:25,700
because we don't have enough money to make alcohol, it's to the point where we can't even take that order.

452
00:50:28,600 --> 00:50:30,700
Is that true?

453
00:50:31,800 --> 00:50:37,900
Why? Because I achieved it, are you riled up?

454
00:50:45,600 --> 00:50:49,600
Please give me money. I need a lot.

455
00:50:49,600 --> 00:50:52,200
I will repay it so lend it.

456
00:50:54,800 --> 00:50:59,200
So, I decided not to take the order.

457
00:51:00,100 --> 00:51:02,600
President, if it's about the money--

458
00:51:02,600 --> 00:51:04,300
No need.

459
00:51:05,600 --> 00:51:09,600
There's no need to consider. The decision has been made.

460
00:51:09,600 --> 00:51:11,000
President.

461
00:51:11,000 --> 00:51:16,400
Don't overdo it. We are not in the situation to be able to handle that order.

462
00:51:18,200 --> 00:51:22,900
I accepted the order.

463
00:51:24,400 --> 00:51:26,900
You accepted the order?

464
00:51:27,600 --> 00:51:29,000
Yes..

465
00:51:30,700 --> 00:51:34,000
What are you planning to do?

466
00:51:34,000 --> 00:51:38,200
I don't have the money to move the lines.

467
00:51:38,200 --> 00:51:41,000
I have maxed out on the loan and there's no way.

468
00:51:41,000 --> 00:51:43,600
I settled it.

469
00:51:43,600 --> 00:51:47,000
We just need to gather a little money.

470
00:51:48,000 --> 00:51:51,200
I went around and begged the family elders.

471
00:51:52,200 --> 00:51:56,000
Elder Dang Sook gave her land deed.

472
00:51:56,000 --> 00:52:00,900
Great grandfather loaned us the money he'd saved to send his grandson to study abroad.

473
00:52:00,900 --> 00:52:02,500
What?

474
00:52:03,600 --> 00:52:05,500
You...

475
00:52:06,400 --> 00:52:10,200
How could you do that without telling me?

476
00:52:10,200 --> 00:52:14,200
The elders, not because of me

477
00:52:19,400 --> 00:52:21,950
but because of Daeseong

478
00:52:23,600 --> 00:52:27,800
when I told the family that it's a way for it to stand up again

479
00:52:27,800 --> 00:52:31,800
they did not hesitate a lot and gave their permission.

480
00:52:34,400 --> 00:52:36,430
Let's do it.

481
00:52:37,300 --> 00:52:42,000
I hope we would do it. We can just do well.

482
00:52:50,200 --> 00:52:54,100
I can find a way for the amount of money we lack.

483
00:53:15,600 --> 00:53:18,300
- Put in four on each side please.
- Yes.

484
00:53:21,200 --> 00:53:24,000
Ahjussi! Please wrap it nicely.

485
00:54:02,800 --> 00:54:06,100
You are working all day at the factory.

486
00:54:06,100 --> 00:54:10,400
What are you doing even late at night?

487
00:54:10,400 --> 00:54:13,200
Do you want to collapse like me?

488
00:54:20,000 --> 00:54:22,600
It's moju. Drink it.

489
00:54:34,200 --> 00:54:36,700
Are you working on yeast again?

490
00:54:38,020 --> 00:54:42,330
Would the fermenting way be the wrong procedure?

491
00:54:44,400 --> 00:54:46,700
What was the problem?

492
00:54:47,700 --> 00:54:49,700
I also don't know.

493
00:54:53,760 --> 00:54:56,450
I really don't know.

494
00:54:58,170 --> 00:55:02,920
Whether it was the wind, the water, the sun,

495
00:55:03,900 --> 00:55:08,400
or if it's the night dew that does it, I really don't know.

496
00:55:10,440 --> 00:55:17,810
But, the yeast you're looking for is everywhere.

497
00:55:18,600 --> 00:55:21,000
Your mom and you

498
00:55:21,000 --> 00:55:26,000
after you both came, the taste of the alcohol has been better.

499
00:55:26,000 --> 00:55:29,500
So the cooperative will definitely rise again.

500
00:55:29,500 --> 00:55:31,400
That's how it was.

501
00:55:33,160 --> 00:55:36,400
The alcohol became deeper.

502
00:55:41,000 --> 00:55:42,820
That...

503
00:55:44,000 --> 00:55:47,000
That's because of the yeast that followed you.

504
00:55:49,400 --> 00:55:52,000
You and your mom

505
00:55:52,000 --> 00:55:56,800
brought it good taste and came to me.

506
00:55:58,800 --> 00:56:00,800
Are you sincere?

507
00:56:01,400 --> 00:56:05,600
Do you think I would be lying?

508
00:56:05,600 --> 00:56:08,400
To look good to you?

509
00:56:09,100 --> 00:56:14,800
Weren't we badly fated mother and daughter?

510
00:56:18,800 --> 00:56:20,400
You...

511
00:56:23,400 --> 00:56:28,600
You... will you call me father even once?

512
00:56:34,300 --> 00:56:36,400
You won't?

513
00:56:49,800 --> 00:56:52,300
If you keep asking me

514
00:56:57,000 --> 00:57:00,400
I... might need to stand and leave.

515
00:57:04,400 --> 00:57:06,400
Okay.

516
00:57:08,010 --> 00:57:12,060
I know how you feel.

517
00:57:33,000 --> 00:57:37,600
King Pigfeet and Bossam.

518
00:57:46,600 --> 00:57:48,500
Welcome.

519
00:58:15,400 --> 00:58:16,900
What is it?

520
00:58:17,800 --> 00:58:22,200
You said you would send money but did not.

521
00:58:22,970 --> 00:58:27,960
You said you would call but did not. You said you would meet me but would not.

522
00:58:28,800 --> 00:58:30,900
I can't take it anymore...

523
00:58:34,100 --> 00:58:36,400
- Coffee please.
- Alright.

524
00:58:45,500 --> 00:58:49,300
I... will not meet you anymore.

525
00:58:50,200 --> 00:58:53,400
You already said that more than a hundred times.

526
00:58:53,400 --> 00:58:55,200
It's true.

527
00:58:55,200 --> 00:58:58,600
You also said that more than a hundred times.

528
00:58:59,570 --> 00:59:04,930
I... will pledge my loyalty to my husband.

529
00:59:06,800 --> 00:59:12,000
You love me but you are loyal to your husband.

530
00:59:12,000 --> 00:59:15,200
I don't care what you do

531
00:59:15,200 --> 00:59:19,600
but being called the same as you

532
00:59:19,600 --> 00:59:23,600
quit it before I rip your mouth.

533
00:59:24,600 --> 00:59:29,200
Wench! Look at how you talk.

534
00:59:29,200 --> 00:59:32,900
Your mouth sure is clean.

535
00:59:34,200 --> 00:59:39,000
If my man dies then you become nothing.

536
00:59:41,500 --> 00:59:43,600
Are you crazy?

537
00:59:43,600 --> 00:59:48,200
It took me a lot to get it. It took me a lot to make it.

538
01:00:07,400 --> 01:00:10,300
So you want me to just buzz off?

539
01:00:13,000 --> 01:00:14,600
Yeah.

540
01:00:15,800 --> 01:00:17,800
Kang Sook.

541
01:00:21,600 --> 01:00:26,200
When I leave, count that money.

542
01:00:26,200 --> 01:00:28,700
You will be satisfied.

543
01:00:29,500 --> 01:00:34,700
It's money I set aside for Eun Jo. I liquidated a huge chunk of it to bring it here.

544
01:00:36,300 --> 01:00:38,600
So don't use it alcohol

545
01:00:38,600 --> 01:00:43,300
Rent a room and live like a person.

546
01:00:44,520 --> 01:00:49,030
You want me to have the money instead of you?

547
01:00:52,800 --> 01:00:55,400
Why are you doing this to me?

548
01:00:57,430 --> 01:01:00,260
What do you see me as?

549
01:01:03,400 --> 01:01:07,600
After I leave, count that money

550
01:01:07,600 --> 01:01:12,800
and if you still want to trade me for that money

551
01:01:13,600 --> 01:01:16,600
then come and catch me.

552
01:01:16,600 --> 01:01:19,000
I will live with you.

553
01:01:47,850 --> 01:01:51,550
₩10,000,000

554
01:02:37,200 --> 01:02:41,700
You... why...

555
01:02:44,600 --> 01:02:48,200
No. I tell you it's not.

556
01:02:48,200 --> 01:02:50,600
No.

557
01:02:50,600 --> 01:02:52,500
What are you denying?

558
01:02:53,400 --> 01:02:57,600
Let's go. I will tell you on the way.

559
01:02:57,600 --> 01:03:00,000
Let's go. I'll tell you everything, okay?

560
01:03:03,600 --> 01:03:07,000
♫ It must be you ♫

561
01:03:07,000 --> 01:03:11,000
♫  I cannot be without you ♫

562
01:03:11,000 --> 01:03:17,600
♫  Like this for another day, month or year ♫

563
01:03:17,600 --> 01:03:21,200
♫  I don't mind even if I am hurt ♫

564
01:03:21,200 --> 01:03:25,200
♫  I don't mind if my heart breaks ♫

565
01:03:25,200 --> 01:03:31,400
♫  because, yes, you are the only one I love. ♫

566
01:03:31,400 --> 01:03:35,000
♫ My bruised heart ♫

567
01:03:35,000 --> 01:03:42,300
♫ is shouting so that I can find you ♫

568
01:03:43,800 --> 01:03:46,300
♫ Wherever you are ♫
